[p27.13] (ARTICLE 42 – FORCE MAJEURE) Neither Party hereto will be considered in default in the performance of its obligations hereunder, to the extent that performance of any such
[p28.1] (ARTICLE 42 – FORCE MAJEURE) obligation is prevented and/or delayed by any cause, existing or future, beyond the control of such Party, and which by that Party’s exercise of due diligence and foresight could not reasonably have been avoided (“Impacted Party”) including, without limitation, the following force majeure events (“Force Majeure Events”): (a) acts of God;
[p28.2] (ARTICLE 42 – FORCE MAJEURE) (b) flood, fire, earthquake, other potential disaster(s) or catastrophe(s), such as epidemics or pandemics, or explosion;
[p28.3] (ARTICLE 42 – FORCE MAJEURE) (c) war, invasion, hostilities (whether war is declared or not);
[p28.4] (ARTICLE 42 – FORCE MAJEURE) (d) national or regional emergencies;
[p28.5] (ARTICLE 42 – FORCE MAJEURE) and (e) other similar events beyond the reasonable control of the Impacted Party.
